    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nwhen using `vim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,noinsert,fuzzy'`, sometimes the pre selected item is not the first item on the menu. If there is one entry, none is selected, if there are multiple, the second one is. This gets corrected when another key is typed, but even then it seems sometimes a bit inconsistent\n\nadding the `nosort` option in completeopt solves this issue, however I don't want it as sorting gives priority to exact match while still allowing to fuzzy search, which I like.\n\nTesting with the <C-x> menu of default nvim, I couldn't reproduce it, so I believe this is linked to mini.\n\nI cannot reproduce this issue on neovim 0.11.* They might have changed something internally for 0.12\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n    local mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\n    local clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n    -- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\n    vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\n    require('mini.deps').setup()\n\n    vim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,noinsert,fuzzy'\n    require 'mini.completion'.setup()\n    ```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n4. Start typing vim. with the first letter the menu is shown but no item is selected. The second letter corrects this and the item is properly selected. The last letter doesn't change anything. deleting the last 2 letters to be back to 'v' keeps 'vim' entry selected. If the menu had 2 options instead of one, it's the second option that will be selected.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a816ca5-42ef-4345-b815-6b3400c5401f",
