            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis is not an issue with 'mini.completion', but a Neovim (even Vim) upstream. See vim/vim#18802. It manifests in 'mini.completion' because it uses `<C-n>` as a default fallback.\n\nUntil it is resolved, you can fix by adding `nosort` flag to 'completeopt'.",
